    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0589" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4027: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-08T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4772. In connection with instructions to Consul-General Harris in Siberia, the text of which was
                    telegraphed to you today, if you see no objection, please read to Foreign Office
                    following cable from American Consul at Vladivostok. You should now have
                    received a personal letter from me<anchor n="29" xml:id="d506-f1"/> which also
                    bears on this subject and should throw additional light on it.</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram 106, March 3, 3 p.m., from the Consul at
                    Vladivostok, printed <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg473"
                        >page 473</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
